      "id": "claim_61a166b501fd446f988d6e848a8dd094",
      "statement": "Document dirty state is derived from the current buffer versus the content snapshot and saved path from the last successful write, rather than undo-history depth; successful writes clear save errors and external-change state, while a new nonexistent target starts modified without a saved snapshot.",
